Sval: package sval-folder beside the browser binary

sval-folder is the program the browser starts to read and write the shared
folder, so a read stuck on a hung network mount stalls it and never the
browser. The browser runs it from beside its own binary and cannot sync a
shared folder without it, and the manifest copies only the files it names.

An instrumented build for profile-guided optimisation packages before
anything stages the program, and its profile run never starts it, so the
manifest names it only outside MOZ_PROFILE_GENERATE.

diff --git a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
index 530b0e9..33f7c49 100644
--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -425,6 +425,12 @@ bin/libfreebl_64int_3.so
 @BINPATH@/sval-mcp@BIN_SUFFIX@
 #endif
 
+; [ sval-folder, the helper that reads and writes Sval's shared folder ]
+;
+#ifndef MOZ_PROFILE_GENERATE
+@BINPATH@/sval-folder@BIN_SUFFIX@
+#endif
+
 ; [ Native Messaging Host Proxy ]
 ;
 #if defined(XP_WIN) || defined(XP_MACOSX)
